      "standardized_narrative": "Syndicate 1200 reported a material strengthening of reserves in 2017, with management stating an overall deterioration of GBP 53.7m. The syndicate cites a combination of factors: a very active US catastrophe year (Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria, California wildfires and a Mexico earthquake) and adverse development in short-tail classes (US Direct & Facultative, Cargo, Yachts & Hull) where prolonged rate pressure and increased facilities led to higher-than-expected losses and IBNR recalibration. The aggregate gross claims outstanding increased materially year-on-year, with most reserve increases concentrated in Property and Reinsurance acceptance exposures.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "The very disappointing underlying performance in 2017 has been impacted by the worst year for catastrophes in the US for over a decade with Hurricanes Harvey, Irma and Maria, the wildfires in California and earthquakes in Mexico causing insured market losses of $135 billion, the costliest year on record (source: Munich Re).",
        "Syndicate 1200 has also had to strengthen loss reserves predominantly in short tail lines of business that have seen the most rate pressure in the market over the last four years, namely US Direct & Facultative, Cargo, Yachts & Hull.",
